[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @verification

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
How each requirement in ``docs/requirements/dashboard/`` is verified. Automated tests run with ``./gradlew testDebugUnitTest`` in ``dashboard_app/``.
<<<

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Display

[VERIFICATION]
UID: VER-DSH-006
METHOD: Demonstration
TITLE: Refused completion is shown
STATEMENT: >>>
With the tablet logged in, tap 'done' on a task the server refuses to complete (for example against a backend without REQ-BE-024, for a person the tablet account does not manage). Expected: the task shows as open again and a message says it may not be completed. With the network disconnected, the message says completing failed.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Not automated: needs Android UI. Not yet performed.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-DSH-022
  ROLE: Verifies

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Data refresh

[VERIFICATION]
UID: VER-DSH-001
METHOD: Demonstration
TITLE: Change check every minute
STATEMENT: >>>
With the tablet connected over USB, follow ``adb logcat`` for at least three minutes while nothing changes. Expected: one ``GET /api/dashboard/etag`` per minute and no ``/api/dashboard`` or ``/api/mobile/tasks`` requests.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Passed on 2026-11-15 on the Galaxy Tab 2 (debug build of fix/dashboard-live-refresh).
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-DSH-001
  ROLE: Verifies

[VERIFICATION]
UID: VER-DSH-002
METHOD: Demonstration
TITLE: Changes appear without restart
STATEMENT: >>>
While following ``adb logcat``, delete, edit and add a task or agenda item in the mobile app or web admin. Expected: after the next etag check the app requests ``/api/dashboard`` and ``/api/mobile/tasks`` and the change is visible on screen.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Passed on 2026-11-15 on the Galaxy Tab 2.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-DSH-002
  ROLE: Verifies

[VERIFICATION]
UID: VER-DSH-003
METHOD: Inspection
TITLE: Week rollover
STATEMENT: >>>
Review ``DashboardViewModel.rollOverToNewWeekIfNeeded``: when the Monday of today changes and the shown week was the previous current week, the shown week becomes the new current week.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Not automated: the view model needs Android. Candidate for a test once the week logic is extracted.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-DSH-003
  ROLE: Verifies

[VERIFICATION]
UID: VER-DSH-004
METHOD: Test
TITLE: Request chunks and cache retention
STATEMENT: >>>
Week lists are split into chunks of at most 12 weeks, gaps and duplicates are handled, and only weeks near today or the viewed week are kept.
<<<
TEST: >>>
dashboard_app/app/src/test/java/nl/buddyplan/display/data/WeekDatesTest.kt: chunksFitTheBackendRangeLimit, chunksSplitOnGapsAndDropDuplicates, keepsWeeksNearTodayOrTheViewedWeek
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-DSH-004
  ROLE: Verifies

[VERIFICATION]
UID: VER-DSH-005
METHOD: Inspection
TITLE: Failed refresh is reported
STATEMENT: >>>
Review ``DataRepository.refreshWeeksAndTasks``: any failed chunk makes the whole refresh return ``Failed``, so ``DashboardSyncManager`` keeps the cached data and reports ``ConnectionState.Offline``.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: REQ-DSH-005
